# GovGuide-AI — Architecture

A bilingual (English / Amharic) web app that explains Ethiopian government services.
A user asks a question in either language; the app identifies which service they
need, asks a clarifying question when the request is ambiguous, and returns a
checklist of required documents, fees, offices, and steps drawn from a curated
knowledge base.

The value of this product is that its answers are correct. An invented fee or a
wrong office sends someone on a wasted trip across a city. Accuracy outranks
coverage, fluency, and speed.

## Stack (do not substitute without discussion)

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui (radix base), Lucide icons |
| AI | Vercel AI SDK v7 via OpenRouter, structured output, Zod schemas |
| Database | PostgreSQL via Drizzle ORM + Drizzle Kit |
| Localization | next-intl, locales `en` and `am` |
| Knowledge | YAML files under `knowledge/`, validated by Zod at build time |
| Runtime | Node.js 22+, npm |
| Deployment | Render, a single Web Service, a single repository |

## Everything lives in the one Next.js app

There is no separate backend. Server code belongs in `app/api/*`, Server Actions
under `actions/`, and plain modules under `lib/`, `services/`, `repositories/`,
and `db/`. Do not add Express, Hono, FastAPI, a Go service, microservices, or
serverless functions outside Next.js. Do not add Prisma (Drizzle exists), Yup
(Zod exists), or a second CSS framework (Tailwind exists).

## Layering

Route handlers and Server Actions are thin. They validate input, call a service,
and shape the response. Business logic lives in `services/`. Database access is
confined to `repositories/`. Nothing outside `repositories/` imports `db/`.

## Knowledge is not stored in the database, and not in the model

`knowledge/services/*.yaml` is the single source of truth for every government
fact. PostgreSQL stores only runtime data: sessions, messages, saved checklists,
feedback, and the AI cache. If Postgres were wiped, no government knowledge would
be lost. The LLM stores nothing; see the AI grounding rule.

## Next.js 16 specifics that differ from earlier versions

These are verified against the bundled docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.
Read those docs before writing Next.js code; training data for this version is
unreliable.

- The middleware file is named `proxy.ts` and exports `proxy`, not `middleware`.
  It runs on the Node.js runtime, which cannot be changed.
- `params` and `searchParams` are Promises everywhere and must be awaited.
  Synchronous access was removed, not merely deprecated.
- `cookies()` from `next/headers` is async. Cookies **cannot be set during
  Server Component rendering** — only in a Server Action, a Route Handler, or
  via `NextResponse.cookies` in `proxy.ts`.
- `error.tsx` and `global-error.tsx` must be Client Components and receive
  `{ error, unstable_retry }`. The prop is not called `reset`.
- Turbopack is the default bundler. `next lint` no longer exists; run `eslint`.
